The market also has a small flower stall.
I stop to look.
I would like something bright in the grey winter.
I spot some beautiful yellow tulips.
Their colour is so warm and happy.
"How much do they cost?" I ask.
"Thirty kroner for the bouquet," the seller answers.
That is a good price.
"I will take those," I say.
He wraps the tulips in paper.
I carefully put them in my bag.
